### Auth — try it from VS Code (REST Client) or Rider/Visual Studio. The client keeps the refresh cookie for you.
### Run it first: `docker compose up --build`. App: http://localhost:8080
@base = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Sign in — access token in the body, refresh token in an HttpOnly cookie
# @name login
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "user@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-battery" }

### 2. Call the API with the access token
GET {{base}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3. Admin only → 403 for this user
GET {{base}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. Refresh: new access token, and the refresh cookie is replaced (rotation)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/refresh

### 5. Active sessions (one per device)
GET {{base}}/api/auth/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6. The public key other services use to validate tokens
GET {{base}}/.well-known/jwks.json

### 7. Weak passwords are refused
POST {{base}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "dana@example.com", "password": "password1234" }

### 8. Sign out
POST {{base}}/api/auth/logout
